course: dictionary
lesson: 10977
title: Wardrobe: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which one the writer means. «Jess tidied by stuffing everything into the wardrobe.» You stuff things into a cupboard, so here a wardrobe is a tall cupboard.
explain: Your wardrobe can also mean all the clothes you own. Ask yourself: is the sentence about the cupboard, or about the clothes? «A winter wardrobe» means your winter clothes, not a cupboard.
explain: In a theatre, the wardrobe is the department that keeps and makes the costumes. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Wardrobe is a noun: one wardrobe, two wardrobes.
fact: «Wardrobe» means a tall cupboard where you hang clothes.
fact: «Wardrobe» also means all the clothes you own, as in «a winter wardrobe».
fact: In a theatre, the wardrobe is the department that keeps and makes the costumes.
fact: In «The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe», children walk through a wardrobe into Narnia.
exercise: «Jess tidied by stuffing everything into the wardrobe.» What is a wardrobe here? | *A tall cupboard where you hang clothes | A bed for the night | A lion in a famous story | A theatre department that makes costumes
exercise: Leo says «a winter wardrobe» means a tall cupboard. Is he right? | No, it means a lion from a story | *No, it means all the winter clothes you own | Yes, it means a tall cupboard for winter | Yes, it means a cold room
exercise: In a theatre, what does «the wardrobe» mean? | The seats at the back of the hall | The stage where the actors perform | *The department that keeps and makes the costumes | The tall cupboard where you hang clothes
test: «Ruby danced like a wardrobe falling down the stairs.» Why does the writer compare her dad to a wardrobe? | Because he was small and very quiet | *Because he moved in a big, heavy, clumsy way | Because he likes sorting clothes | Because he hid under the bed
test: Which sentence uses wardrobe to mean all your clothes? | «A big box was hidden on top of the wardrobe.» | *«Mum bought me a new winter wardrobe.» | «The lion walked out of the wardrobe.» | «The wardrobe door was squeaky.»
exam: «A big box is hidden on top of the wardrobe.» What does wardrobe mean here? | *A tall cupboard | All the clothes you own | A lion from Narnia | The theatre department that makes costumes
